00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:01,040
Here is the first one.

107
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,600
Our scout master says it's his job

108
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:07,520
to decide who goes to national youth leadership training each year

109
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:08,560
from the troop

110
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:13,040
and which of the training courses they should go to.

111
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:15,760
Our committee says they decide who goes

112
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,200
and where they can go,

113
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:21,120
since they're the ones that cover the costs for the scouts attending.

114
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:23,440
Do you know of any official materials

115
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,680
that can help us figure out who decides

116
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,360
who goes to the training,

117
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:29,680
where they go and who pays?

118
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,880
Well, probably not going to be able to help you

119
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:37,360
find anything that specific in policy,

120
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:41,600
but we can certainly talk about some generalities

121
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,920
that may help inform the situation

122
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:46,719
And just to broaden the scope of the whole thing.

123
00:07:46,719 --> 00:07:48,400
you know, when decisions like this

124
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,800
devolve into a turf battle between adults,

125
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:53,680
it indicates that something's kind of out of whack

126
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:56,400
in their basic understanding and attitudes.

127
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:58,880
We're not commanding officers or bosses

128
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:01,040
and scouts aren't soldiers or employees

129
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,400
that we order around.

130
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:05,280
So if a scout wants to go to national youth leadership training

131
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,640
and they come to me and they say,

132
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:08,480
hey, yeah, I want to do this training,

133
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:10,400
I would say, well, more power to you.

134
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,480
Do you know where you're going? and everything like that.

135
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:15,200
Yep, Yep, Okay, Great, Go for it,

136
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,680
And I suppose I could recommend a course.

137
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,360
It's really none of my business,

138
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:21,680
And if you were fortunate enough to be in an area

139
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:26,320
that had several choices of courses, locations and times,

140
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,840
and they asked me to recommend one.

141
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:28,720
I suppose I could,

142
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:31,760
And whether or not they took my recommendation on that

143
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,840
is totally up to them, and their parents

144
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,000
doesn't really make a difference to me

145
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,559
Now, because the troop is paying for the course.

146
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:41,039
it would seem to me, in the event of difference of opinion

147
00:08:41,039 --> 00:08:43,600
the committee would take precedence over the scout master,

148
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,400
because that's just the way troops are ran.

149
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:49,280
just the committee chair can appoint or remove a scout master

150
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:50,960
as they see fit, with the consent

151
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:53,200
of the chartered organization representative.

152
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,800
So if we want to have a turf war,

153
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,240
the committee chair is going to win.

154
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:58,880
Let's not have a turf war, because turf war

155
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,760
always result in a negative effect on scouts

156
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:03,680
and on the program as a whole.

157
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:06,720
Boy, it just saps everybody's energy right away from them.

158
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:09,040
So resolving this particular question

159
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,360
probably goes a little deeper than who's in charge

160
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,280
or who gets to decide what.

161
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:15,840
I think there's just like a basic misunderstanding

162
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,120
of what scouting is about.

163
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:20,720
I'm not really interested in that level of control,

164
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,160
to tell you the truth.

165
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:25,440
So this second email begins this way:

166
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,360
My son was a Cub Scout.

167
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,800
I helped as a den leader

168
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:32,400
