169
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:34,800
and became an assistant scout master.

170
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:36,160
My son's moving along.

171
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:38,800
He's earned first class. after a couple of years

172
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,960
I didn't realize how much I had missed scouting.

173
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:42,560
I was a scout myself

174
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:46,320
and I think I'll likely stay on doing this work.

175
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:49,760
I would even say that I would stay on with this troop

176
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,040
after he ages out.

177
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,960
That's how much I enjoy being a volunteer.

178
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:55,440
We're a small troop right now, but we're growing.

179
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:56,720
and here's my question:

180
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:59,280
As much as my son and I enjoy it,

181
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:02,640
our troop is as disorganized as one can be.

182
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,200
The scout master and his assistants

183
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,040
have been around for a couple of decades,

184
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:09,840
yet they seem to do everything by the seat of their pants.

185
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:12,080
The adults do create an annual schedule,

186
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:14,720
but many times the locations of the trips

187
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:17,120
aren't finalized as late as a week or two

188
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:17,920
before the trip,

189
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:20,800
and this kind of thing drives me crazy.

190
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:23,360
The troop is definitely not youth led

191
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,040
and I really didn't realize this

192
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:28,400
until I went to training to be an assistant scout master.

193
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,400
The scout master makes all the patrols,

194
00:10:30,959 --> 00:10:32,400
assigns the patrol leaders

195
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:34,400
and even created the patrol names.

196
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,439
The scouts are young,

197
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,240
so there's no senior patrol leader.

198
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,240
I suspect the scout master would probably

199
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:42,079
choose who was senior patrol leader

200
00:10:42,079 --> 00:10:43,280
if we did have one.

201
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,400
Make no mistake,

202
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,480
the scout master and the other

203
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:49,199
scouters involved with the troop are good men.

204
00:10:49,199 --> 00:10:50,560
They're easy to get along with,

205
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,599
They care for the scouts.

206
00:10:51,599 --> 00:10:54,480
They just prefer to lead the troop themselves.

207
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:56,560
I've suggested changes before.

208
00:10:56,560 --> 00:10:58,320
They seem to be willing to listen,

209
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:01,120
but I sense they're not willing to actually

210
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:03,760
implement any significant changes.

211
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:06,960
We anticipate a large group of weevilos joining soon,

212
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:09,760
so I'm interested in at least discussing changes

213
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:12,480
that would be more faithful to the patrol method.

214
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:15,200
How do you think I should approach the scout master with this,

215
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:17,120
since it would be a significant change?

216
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:20,720
If they sounded agreeable, what would we do next?

217
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,800
I've listened to several podcasts about this,

218
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:25,200
but they're more conceptual than directive.

219
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:27,760
I was hoping for more detail,

220
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,160
Kind of like an order of events.

221
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:34,320
Well, first, I'm glad you're finding the podcast useful

222
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:37,680
and I'm glad you got in touch with me,

223
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:40,160
because what's happened to you

224
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:42,400
has happened to a lot of assistant scout masters

225
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,840
who've sent me similar questions.

226
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:46,560
You've run across this guy online

227
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:50,240
who has a podcast and a particular vision of scouting

228
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:53,200
that doesn't correspond to what you see in your troop

229
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,640
and you want to change things around.

230
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:58,080
So my standard advice when I get a question like this

231
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:00,640
is I usually tell people to find another troop

232
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:03,600
that more closely corresponds to what they'd like to have

233
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:06,400
for their son. but that doesn't seem to be an option here,

234
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:08,880
and I understand. my second piece of advice-

235
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:10,640
I don't think is an option here either,

236
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,160
which is, you know, start a troop.

237
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,720
If you can't find a troop that isn't operating

238
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:17,040
the way that you think it ought to operate,

239
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,880
well, look into starting one,

240
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:22,000
and that's never really a very popular option.

241
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,480
So if neither of these things appeal to you,

242
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:27,439
the next thing I have to do is ask you

243
00:12:27,439 --> 00:12:29,360
why you want to change things

244
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:32,000
Now. there's no indication that any young people

245
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,360
are actually being harmed by the adults involved,

246
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:38,160
no undercurrent of general dissatisfaction

247
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:41,360
or, and perhaps more importantly,

248
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:44,320
a shared notion that things need changing.

249
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:47,360
Now you'd note that things aren't quite as organized

250
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,640
as you like, and I gotta tell you

251
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:52,400
that's not unusual. besides, if you change things around,

252
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,560
you'll be trading one form of frustrating

253
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:56,080
disorganization for another.

254
00:12:56,800 --> 00:13:01,920
There is no such thing as frustration. free scouting-

255
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,880
You may quote me

256
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,600
So from what you've told me about your,

257
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,680
the troop and your experiences-

258
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:11,600
is: the troop is having regular meetings,

259
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:14,240
they're going camping and scouts are advancing,

260
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:16,319
so it's functioning and serving the interests

261
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:18,960
of scouts at least in some measure correct.

262
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:22,320
Obviously, if an adult does all the leading,

263
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:24,960
it denies a number of opportunities to the scouts.

264
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:28,640
but you know this is far more common

265
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:31,760
than youth led troops, at least in my experience.

266
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:34,400
While the adult led model is not optimal,

267
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:37,360
it does not do objective harm,

268
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:40,960
It just denies scouts are more expansive

269
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:44,560
and I guess some would say authentic scouting experience.

270
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:47,520
I guess if I wanted to be really hard-nosed I would say that

271
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:50,560
you know, without the patrol method in operating

272
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:52,320
it's not really scouting.

273
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:54,640
but the real heart of the matter here is

274
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:57,920
the single most important issue

275
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:00,640
is, as an assistant scout master,

276
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:03,280
you're not in a position to lead a series of changes

277
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:07,040
and I'm going to emphasize that.

278
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:10,880
I'm going to repeat it: as an assistant scout master,

279
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:12,640
you're really not in a position

280
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:16,080
to implement a series of changes. you've come into this,

281
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:18,720
you've looked at it, you go: I'm not really satisfied

282
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:20,319
with the way things are going.

283
00:14:20,319 --> 00:14:22,960
I want to change everything around. well, that's kind of like

284
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:25,120
saying: give me the wheel, I want to drive the car

285
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:26,720
when you're in the backseat,

286
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:29,920
Since I'm talking with somebody who's working within the BSA.

287
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:31,600
the way the BSA defines things

288
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,720
is the troops committee chair is more or less

289
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,880
the decision maker and director,

290
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:40,720
but in reality, most of the- a lot of the times,

291
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:42,960
the scout master has pretty broad authority,

292
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,040
makes all the decisions and the committee chair

293
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:46,640
is more in the background.

294
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:50,480
so the scout master is usually going to be the person who

295
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:52,640
decides whether they're going to make changes or not.

296
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:56,720
and absent a shared notion that change is needed

297
00:14:57,440 --> 00:15:00,160
and a shared vision of what the changes ought to be,

298
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:02,960
I don't see a whole lot of potential for change

299
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:05,280
in this or any other situation.

300
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:06,800
but nevertheless,

301
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:10,080
nothing ventured, nothing gained right, go ahead,

302
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:13,040
make some suggestions, have a discussion with the scout master,

303
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:16,720
see what kind of, see what kind of headway you can make.

304
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:20,400
I don't understand any of the personal dynamics involved

305
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:22,560
and I can't really effectively advise you

306
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,720
on how those suggestions should be made.

307
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:28,640
but if, but, if the scout master is a receptive person

308
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:30,640
and they're easy to get along with.

309
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,320
you know, if I were just doing it myself,

310
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:34,160
I'd probably just tell him what I was thinking.

311
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:38,000
I'm not a particularly subtle person.

312
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:40,880
that's the way I would handle it.

313
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:43,200
I would just say: you know, I went to training.

314
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:44,880
they talk about this patrol method.

315
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:46,480
I'd like to discuss that with you

316
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:49,520
and I wonder if you've ever thought about making some changes

317
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:52,080
to bring things more in line with the patrol method.

318
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:54,480
so the only other open issue is: okay,

319
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,800
so let's say that you go to the scout master

320
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:59,360
or the committee chair or whoever

321
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,600
and you make some suggestions about changes

322
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:03,600
and they say, yeah, great, let's do that.

323
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,040
what do you do next?

324
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:07,040
and I'm often asked what kind of

325
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:09,120
you know concrete steps you should take

326
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:12,480
to change from being adult led

327
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,760
to being youth led,

328
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:18,160
and I don't know. I've never really been able to come up

329
00:16:18,160 --> 00:16:19,839
with a step-by-step list,

330
00:16:19,839 --> 00:16:20,959
although I've tried.

331
00:16:20,959 --> 00:16:23,280
but of course, the crucial first thing

332
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:24,240
that would have to happen

333
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:27,199
is all the adults involved have to be on the same page.

334
00:16:27,199 --> 00:16:29,680
they have to agree what this is going to look like.

335
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:32,719
after that, there's really no secret formula.

336
00:16:32,719 --> 00:16:34,240
you talk to your scouts,

337
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,800
you tell them what the changes are going to be,

338
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:39,040
you stop doing things one way

339
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,360
and you start doing things another way,

340
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,680
and scouts are reasonably flexible

341
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:44,880
with this kind of thing.

342
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,160
but you know you're going to go through

343
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:48,320
a longish period of transition

344
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:51,520
before you get to the point where you have

345
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:54,720
exchanged one set of frustrations for another one-

346
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:57,360
and you know I do get this kind of question

347
00:16:57,360 --> 00:17:00,320
on a fairly regular basis.

348
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,280
I am in a troop.

349
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:03,360
I'm not happy with the way it's going.

350
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:04,960
I would like to change things

351
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,720
to the way you say they should be going,

352
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,400
because you sound very smart.

353
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:09,920
if you're not in a position

354
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:12,640
in the organizational structure of a troop

355
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,480
to implement changes like this,

356
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:17,600
suggesting them to those that are in those positions

357
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:18,640
is one way to go.

358
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,839
but you have to realize

359
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:22,160
you could just end up being very frustrated

360
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,200
about the whole thing

361
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:26,880
because your suggestions may fall on deaf ears.

362
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:29,200
that's why I say: you know,

363
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,400
either find a troop

364
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:31,920
that corresponds more closely

365
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,120
to the way you think things

366
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:33,680
ought to be done

367
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:35,200
or start one yourself,

368
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,800
because the chance your frustrations

369
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,600
are going to go away

370
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,680
because of some suggestions that you make,

371
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:41,920
I don't know-

372
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:43,600
doesn't seem to be like

373
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,760
a high probability strategy to me.

374
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:48,320
so this last email answer

375
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:50,240
is actually an answer to an email question,

376
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,560
but there's no real reason to read the whole email.

377
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,400
here's the story

378
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:56,080
I heard from a scout master who said

379
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:57,600
that they were kind of frustrated.

380
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:00,000
they're relatively new to the work

381
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,080
and they were encountering the usual things

382
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:03,040
that we encounter:

383
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:05,680
parents who were perhaps

384
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,840
used to being a little over involved in things,

385
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:10,080
a troop that wasn't functioning as he wanted.

386
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:11,600
you know

387
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:13,680
the the kind of thing that we pretty much

388
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:15,200
live with all the time.

389
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:16,879
they sent me a very long email.

390
00:18:16,879 --> 00:18:18,720
they had written to the troops families,

391
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:20,560
kind of laying things out

392
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,399
in a once for all kind of fashion,

393
00:18:22,399 --> 00:18:24,080
making some big statements,

394
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:25,120
and- and

395
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,639
you know what I mean. right,

396
00:18:26,639 --> 00:18:28,320
the most of us have written,

397
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,159
have written that email

398
00:18:30,159 --> 00:18:31,920
at least once before.

399
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:34,480
they wanted me to review the email,

400
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:36,240
comment on how it could be improved.

401
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,120
and here is

402
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:39,120
the way that I replied.

403
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:40,880
since you asked,

404
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:43,760
I'm going to be very plain and direct.

405
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:45,360
don't mistake this for criticism.

406
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:46,800
it's because it's intended

407
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,560
in the best spirit possible.

408
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,880
I would never suggest sending an email

409
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:51,360
like this.

410
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:52,880
it has much more potential

411
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,160
for harm than good.

412
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,880
so whoever's on your side

413
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:57,760
in these issues

414
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,120
will look it over

415
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:00,880
and soon forget what you've said.

416
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,800
the opposition

417
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:05,920
will find plenty of leverage

418
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:08,000
to argue about what you've written.

419
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,760
they'll reread and dissect it

420
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:11,440
and discuss it amongst themselves,

421
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,080
and the neutral faction

422
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:16,480
will not read it very much at all.

423
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:18,240
they may scan it a little bit

424
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,680
and you're going to find that

425
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:20,960
all three of those reactions,

426
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:22,640
rather than helping you

427
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:23,920
sort out, your frustrations

428
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:26,080
are just going to be more frustrating.

429
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:26,320
so

430
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:27,680
look,

431
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:28,560
in my experience,

432
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:31,440
parents do not read things like this.

433
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:34,080
they don't really read things like

434
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,760
you know- a troop policy manual-

435
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:36,639
if you have one

436
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:39,600
and you don't really want to have one-

437
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:42,000
they don't really read

438
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:43,760
much of anything

439
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,679
in order to attempt to understand

440
00:19:45,679 --> 00:19:46,560
what is going on.

441
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:49,360
that's not necessarily a criticism,

442
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:51,040
that's just an observation

443
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,800
based on my experience.

444
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:54,399
a lot of times parents are not all

445
00:19:54,399 --> 00:19:56,399
that interested in delving down

446
00:19:56,399 --> 00:19:58,320
into the specifics of stuff like that,

447
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:00,560
but when something happens

448
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:02,720
that challenges what they assume

449
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:03,840
ought to happen,

450
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:06,320
that's when they start to get vocal

451
00:20:06,879 --> 00:20:08,639
and then you explain

452
00:20:08,639 --> 00:20:10,399
why you're doing what you're doing

453
00:20:10,399 --> 00:20:12,639
and you have to deal with these issues

454
00:20:12,639 --> 00:20:14,720
over and over and over again

455
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:15,440
individually,

456
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,679
one parent at a time,

457
00:20:17,679 --> 00:20:19,679
because often husbands and wives

458
00:20:19,679 --> 00:20:21,040
don't even end up discussing

459
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:22,800
what you have told one or another.

460
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:24,240
so this never goes away.

461
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,840
it's a feature of our work.

462
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:26,800
it's not a flaw

463
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:28,159
that can be fixed by

464
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,600
writing email

465
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:32,400
or putting out a troop policy manual

466
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:35,280
or having extensive

467
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:37,200
introductory meetings.

468
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:38,960
this is just one of the costs

469
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:40,720
of doing business as a scouter.

470
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:42,000
this never goes away,

471
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:43,600
never, ever.

472
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:44,960
now, that's not to say that

473
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:46,720
you shouldn't make sure to offer

474
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:49,600
information to families

475
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:51,360
so that they can understand things.

476
00:20:51,360 --> 00:20:52,560
all I'm saying is

477
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:54,800
I wouldn't look at the offer

478
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:56,400
of that information

479
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,880
as a high percentage solution

480
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:01,280
to solving your frustrations.

481
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:03,040
now, if you do want some advice

482
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:04,880
on how to get things

483
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,560
more energized and rolling

484
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:08,000
in a better direction,

485
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,440
I'll repeat what I said

486
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:11,680
in an earlier email answer.

487
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,200
the way troops are constituted

488
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,400
in the in the BSA,

489
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:15,520
the committee chair

490
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:17,520
is the central decision maker

491
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:18,960
bound to carry out the policies

492
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:20,400
and procedures of the BSA

493
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:21,680
that shape the program.

494
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:23,840
this is not a democratic process.

495
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:25,280
it's not subject to the opinion

496
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:27,280
of parents or other volunteers,

497
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:28,480
and I would never introduce

498
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:29,600
the idea that it is.

499
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:31,600
we don't sit down and litigate

500
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:33,040
the elements of the program.

501
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:34,080
they're presented to us.

502
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:35,200
we carry them out.

503
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,240
and I'm not saying that

504
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:37,840
scouting is autocratic

505
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:40,480
because it is a team sport.

506
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,760
it's just, like

507
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,680
Baden Powell said,

508
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:46,000
a jolly game, right,

509
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,200
and that depends on

510
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:49,120
family scouts and scouts

511
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:50,240
working together

512
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:52,000
in a collaborative process.

513
00:21:52,639 --> 00:21:54,639
when people understand their roles

514
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:56,240
in that process

515
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:58,000
or their positions on the team

516
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,680
that plays this jolly game,

517
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:02,080
then things get energized.

518
00:22:02,080 --> 00:22:03,440
so if I were in your shoes

519
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,440
and I felt like things weren't going

520
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:06,800
quite according to plan

521
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:08,240
and I was frustrated.

522
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,040
I would sit down

523
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:10,160
with my committee chair

524
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:12,720
and assure that you both have

525
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:14,560
each other's unquestioning support

526
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:16,639
and shared understanding

527
00:22:16,639 --> 00:22:18,399
of how things move forward.

528
00:22:18,399 --> 00:22:19,440
if you can't achieve

529
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:20,720
this kind of understanding,

530
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:21,520
well, reconsider.

531
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:22,560
if this is a group of people

532
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,160
you want to continue to work with,

533
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,280
if you can arrive

534
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:26,480
at a good working agreement

535
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:27,520
with your committee chair,

536
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,240
then move on.

537
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:30,320
when someone challenges

538
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:31,120
what you're doing,

539
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:33,280
tell them the basis of your actions,

540
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:35,280
ask them to follow your lead.

541
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:36,400
you and the committee chair

542
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:37,440
are the leader

543
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:40,000
of the other adult volunteers.

544
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,080
they take direction from you,

545
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:44,320
not the other way around.

546
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:45,520
so when there's a decision

547
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:46,080
to be made,

548
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:48,160
they're looking for your leadership.

549
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:50,480
although it is a collaborative process,

550
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:51,520
although

551
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:53,760
we do our best to seek consensus,

552
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,360
there has to be people

553
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:56,560
who make decisions

554
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:57,840
and who are leading

555
00:22:57,840 --> 00:22:59,920
the other adult volunteers.

556
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:01,280
so the author of that email

557
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:02,240
got back to me and said:

558
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:03,440
I value your honesty

559
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:04,560
and straightforward advice.

560
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:05,680
I'm going to start writing

561
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,880
letters like this

562
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:07,920
more often

563
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,440
and keep them to myself.

564
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,200
it was very cathartic

565
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:12,320
and it helped me sort out

566
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:14,320
my thoughts and frustrations.

567
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:15,680
well, I would encourage

568
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:16,640
everyone to do that.

569
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,640
write as much as you want

570
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:19,840
about why you're doing

571
00:23:19,840 --> 00:23:20,640
what you're doing

572
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:21,760
and the frustrations

573
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:22,720
that you encounter.

574
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:25,280
write them as a letter to yourself

575
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:26,480
that

576
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:29,040
no one will ever see.

577
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:31,360
it is a useful cathartic

578
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:33,200
as well as a way to refine

579
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,000
your approach

580
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,520
and to deal with the common

581
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:37,360
frustrations that we all deal with.

582
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:39,200
I started doing that

583
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:42,080
a long, long time ago

584
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:44,480
and then I started the blog,

585
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:47,600
and the rest is history, I suppose,

586
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:49,200
is what they say right.

587
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:50,160
this scouter

588
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,520
was dealing with

589
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:53,120
frustrations he was having

590
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:54,320
with parents,

591
00:23:54,320 --> 00:23:55,840
misunderstanding

592
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:57,440
or being a little over involved

593
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:58,639
in what was going on.

594
00:23:58,639 --> 00:23:59,760
so now this is going to

595
00:23:59,760 --> 00:24:00,879
sound kind of cranky,

596
00:24:00,879 --> 00:24:03,200
but I think it's reasonably accurate.

597
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:05,360
95% of the problems

598
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:07,040
we encounter as scouts

599
00:24:07,040 --> 00:24:08,320
are going to originate

600
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:10,320
with our scouts families,

601
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:12,240
their parents specifically,

602
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:13,920
the 5% of the problems

603
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:15,120
that we have that originate

604
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:15,840
with scouts

605
00:24:15,840 --> 00:24:17,840
are usually exacerbated

606
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:19,520
by the involvement of their parents.

607
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,360
scouts themselves

608
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:22,960
are not all that hard to work with.

609
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:24,480
usually you can solve things

610
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:25,200
with scouts,

611
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:25,920
but parents

612
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:28,160
it's a little more difficult.

613
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:30,000
now, just in case that sounds bitter

614
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:31,120
or cynical,

615
00:24:31,120 --> 00:24:32,880
I want to explain that it isn't.

616
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:34,560
it's just the reality of working

617
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:35,360
with young people.

618
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:36,160
it's been that way

619
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:37,440
since the whole thing started.

620
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:38,960
it will continue to be that way

621
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:40,320
for the foreseeable future.

622
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:41,200
you can go back

623
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:42,560
as far as you want

624
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:44,080
in scouting literature

625
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:46,320
anywhere at any time,

626
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:47,120
and you're going to find

627
00:24:47,120 --> 00:24:48,640
that people encounter

628
00:24:48,640 --> 00:24:50,800
these same frustrations.

629
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:52,960
the world isn't going to hell in a handbasket.

630
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:55,200
there's not been this massive sea change

631
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,879
about the attitudes that parents have

632
00:24:56,879 --> 00:24:58,080
when it comes to volunteers

633
00:24:58,080 --> 00:24:59,200
who are dealing with their children.

634
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:01,760
this is just the way things have been

635
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:04,000
and the way that they will continue to be.

636
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:05,440
it's an important part

637
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:07,360
of your work as a scouter.

638
00:25:07,360 --> 00:25:08,879
the real problem seems to be

639
00:25:08,879 --> 00:25:11,200
we don't prepare our volunteers

640
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:13,040
to work with families

641
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:14,800
as well as we prepare them

642
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:16,240
to work with scouts.

643
00:25:16,240 --> 00:25:17,600
you know we do a pretty good job

644
00:25:17,600 --> 00:25:18,800
of familiarizing people

645
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:20,399
with the policies and procedures

646
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:21,680
of the organization,

647
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:23,440
the important points of the goals

648
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:25,040
and the methods of scouting

649
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:27,360
and a lot of logistical information,

650
00:25:27,360 --> 00:25:29,200
but we usually leave the development

651
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,800
of the soft skills

652
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:33,120
that are needed to deal with

653
00:25:33,120 --> 00:25:35,760
the frustrations that you're going to have

654
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:37,440
in dealing with scouts families.

655
00:25:37,440 --> 00:25:39,200
we kind of leave that up to you.

656
00:25:39,200 --> 00:25:41,200
so i want to hear about your general

657
